{{!-- A1's body: the lead story with its companions, then the archive grid.

	{{> "home/latest" feed=feed}}

The two bands are partials of their own because each carries a treatment that depends on what the
publication actually has — see home/lead-block.hbs for the imageless lead and
home/archive-grid.hbs for the sparse grid. This partial is the section, its heading, the tag
strip, and the one decision that sizes both bands.

Position 1 is the cover, so the bands below start at 2: the lead story, its companions at 3–5, and
6–14 in the grid — UNLESS the lead band is omitted, in which case the grid runs 2–14 instead.

WHEN THE LEAD BAND IS OMITTED, AND WHY THE GRID'S SLICE MOVES WITH IT. A publication with no
photographs has nothing for the lead band to lead with: home/lead-block.hbs already sets it as
type when its own post has no image, and on a Day-one publication that band is four posts of
running text above nine more of the same. So when the newest five posts are all imageless the
band is not drawn at all and the grid absorbs its four posts. The grid MUST absorb them: the
window and the `/` collection are both fourteen (home/window.hbs), so a layout that draws fewer
than fourteen re-opens the pagination hole that number exists to close.

That makes this the one **Underset** (CONTEXT.md) fixed by omitting a band rather than by
rearranging it — allowed only because no post dies, since the band's four reappear as cards.
docs/adr/0005 records it.

HOW THE CONDITION IS COMPUTED, WHICH IS THE AWKWARD PART. Handlebars cannot ask "did any of these
four posts have an image": {{#foreach}} has no accumulator and {{#has any="feature_image"}} answers
only for one post. NQL can express it as a date cutoff — no post newer than the oldest of the
four carries an image — so the decision is one extra {{#get}} whose only job is to come back
empty. Three things about it, each of which cost a probe run:

- `from="2" limit="4"`, NOT `to="5"`. Ghost's foreach sets `@last` on `current === to`
  (core/frontend/helpers/foreach.js), so `to="5"` never fires it on a publication with fewer than
  five posts and the whole decision would render nothing. With `limit`, `to` falls back to the
  window's length, so `@last` lands on position 5 or on the oldest post there is.
- `{{published_at}}` renders `2026-08-28T09:00:00.000+00:00`, and the `+00:00` is safe only
  because it sits inside the filter's quotes — unquoted, NQL would read the `+` as its own AND.
- The cutoff is `>=`, so the test spans positions 1–5 and the cover is in it. That couples the two
  treatments deliberately: a photographed cover can never sit above a dropped band. Testing 2–5
  alone would need a second date, and a second date can only reach a filter as `{{../published_at}}`,
  which is fatal in Ghost 6 — `IncorrectUsageError: unsupported path segment ""`, answered as a
  200 with a hole in the page.

`{{#if photographed}}` and not the get's `{{else}}`: get calls `options.inverse` only for an
invalid resource or an API error, never for an empty result — and an empty result is the whole
signal here.

`{{#if feed.[1]}}` around the section is the one-post case. With a single post the cover is the
publication and both bands below it are empty, so the heading, its rule and the tag strip would
be chrome over nothing — an **Orphan**, which docs/adr/0003 says to omit. Index access, so it
costs no query.

`../../feed`: {{#get}} renders its block with the query's own response as the context, so from
inside the get the window is two frames up — one for the get, one for the {{#foreach}} it sits
in. ({{#if}} adds no frame; Handlebars pushes one only when the context object changes.) --}}
{{#if feed.[1]}}
	<section
		id="latest"
		aria-labelledby="a1-latest"
		class="container pt-18">
		<div class="border-border mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-7 border-b pb-3.5">
			<h2
				id="a1-latest"
				class="font-display text-h2 tracking-heading font-medium">{{t "Latest"}}</h2>

			{{> "tag-strip"}}
		</div>

		{{#foreach feed from="2" limit="4"}}
			{{#if @last}}
				{{#get "posts" limit="1" filter="published_at:>='{{published_at}}'+feature_image:-null" as |photographed|}}
					{{#if photographed}}
						{{> "home/lead-block" feed=../../feed}}

						{{> "home/archive-grid" feed=../../feed start="6" mt="mt-14"}}
					{{else}}
						{{> "home/archive-grid" feed=../../feed start="2"}}
					{{/if}}
				{{/get}}
			{{/if}}
		{{/foreach}}
	</section>
{{/if}}
